---
import PageLayout from "#/layout/PageLayout.astro";
import Section from "#/components/ui/Section.astro";
import Heading from "#/components/ui/Heading.astro";
import Paragraph from "#/components/ui/Paragraph.astro";
import Explainer from "#/components/ui/Explainer.astro";
import Link from "#/components/Link.astro";
---

<PageLayout title="Jstmemit // Terms of service" canonical="https://jstmemit.com/terms">
    <Section variant="dark" headingId="termsHeading" descriptionId="termsDescription">
        <div slot="text" class="mx-auto mt-30 flex w-full max-w-333 flex-col gap-3">
            <Explainer>Last updated: 5th July, 2026</Explainer>
            <Heading variant="h1" id="termsHeading"> Terms of service </Heading>
            <Paragraph id="termsDescription">
                <b>TL;DR:</b> Jstmemit turns your channel's chats into memes. Memes are auto-generated, so they won't always
                make sense. Use it for fun, don't use it to cause harm.
            </Paragraph>
        </div>
    </Section>

    <Section variant="light" headingId="basicsHeading" descriptionId="basicsDescription">
        <div slot="text" class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-333 flex-col gap-3">
            <Heading id="basicsHeading"> 1. The basics </Heading>
            <Paragraph id="basicsDescription">
                By adding <b>Jstmemit</b> to your server, using the bot, or visiting our website (<a
                    class="text-bubblegum-pink"
                    href="https://jstmemit.com">https://jstmemit.com</a
                >), you're agreeing to these terms and to our <a class="text-bubblegum-pink" href="/privacy"
                    >Privacy policy</a
                >.
            </Paragraph>
        </div>
    </Section>

    <Section variant="dark" headingId="whatItDoesHeading" descriptionId="whatItDoesDescription">
        <div slot="text" class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-333 flex-col gap-3">
            <Heading id="whatItDoesHeading"> 2. What Jstmemit actually does </Heading>
            <Paragraph id="whatItDoesDescription">
                <b>Jstmemit</b> is a Discord bot that makes memes out of your community's conversations. Once it's enabled
                in a channel, it keeps a short memory of recent messages, images and GIFs, and every so often mixes them on
                a meme template.
            </Paragraph>
        </div>
    </Section>

    <Section variant="light" headingId="whoCanUseHeading" descriptionId="whoCanUseDescription">
        <div slot="text" class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-333 flex-col gap-3">
            <Heading id="whoCanUseHeading"> 3. Who can use it </Heading>
            <Paragraph id="whoCanUseDescription">
                To use Jstmemit you need to meet Discord's own minimum age requirement (13 in most places, higher in
                some countries) and be allowed to use Discord where you live.
            </Paragraph>
        </div>
    </Section>

    <Section variant="dark" headingId="enablingHeading" descriptionId="enablingDescription">
        <div slot="text" class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-333 flex-col gap-3">
            <Heading id="enablingHeading"> 4. Enabling the bot </Heading>
            <Paragraph id="enablingDescription">
                Jstmemit does nothing until someone with the "Manage Server" or "Manage Channels" permission runs <b
                    >/enable</b
                > in a channel. If that someone is you, you're confirming you're allowed to turn it on for that server, and
                you're responsible for letting your members know the channel's messages will be used to make memes.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                You can turn it back off with <b>/enable</b> whenever you want, and delete stored data with <b
                    >/settings</b
                >. If you wish to know more about what data we store and our retention policy, please have a look at the <a
                    class="text-bubblegum-pink"
                    href="/privacy">Privacy policy</a
                >.
            </Paragraph>
        </div>
    </Section>

    <Section variant="light" headingId="yourContentHeading" descriptionId="yourContentDescription">
        <div slot="text" class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-333 flex-col gap-3">
            <Heading id="yourContentHeading"> 5. Your content </Heading>
            <Paragraph id="yourContentDescription">
                Jstmemit only works because it can read the messages, images and GIFs in an enabled channel. So by using
                it, you give us permission (non-exclusive, royalty-free licence) to store and use that content for the
                purpose of generating memes.
            </Paragraph>
        </div>
    </Section>

    <Section variant="dark" headingId="prohibitedHeading" descriptionId="prohibitedDescription">
        <div slot="text" class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-333 flex-col gap-3">
            <Heading id="prohibitedHeading"> 6. What you can't do </Heading>
            <Paragraph id="prohibitedDescription">
                Please do not: <ul class="list-[lower-alpha] pl-10 text-white/75">
                    <li>use the bot to make or spread content that's illegal, hateful, harassing or threatening</li>
                    <li>use it to deliberately target, harm or humiliate specific people</li>
                    <li>try to break, overload or gain unauthorized access to the bot or the systems behind it</li>
                    <li>abuse the bot to spam channels</li>
                </ul>
            </Paragraph>
        </div>
    </Section>

    <Section variant="light" headingId="reportingHeading" descriptionId="reportingDescription">
        <div slot="text" class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-333 flex-col gap-3">
            <Heading id="reportingHeading"> 7. Reporting a problem </Heading>
            <Paragraph id="reportingDescription">
                If you believe a meme is offensive, infringes someone's rights, or you've just found a bug, tell us on
                our <a
                    href="https://discord.gg/THRnn8fhkZ"
                    target="_blank"
                    class="text-bubblegum-pink"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer">Support server</a
                > or email <a class="text-bubblegum-pink" href="mailto:contact@jstmemit.com">contact@jstmemit.com</a>.
            </Paragraph>
        </div>
    </Section>

    <Section variant="dark" headingId="noGuaranteesHeading" descriptionId="noGuaranteesDescription">
        <div slot="text" class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-333 flex-col gap-3">
            <Heading id="noGuaranteesHeading"> 8. No guarantees </Heading>
            <Paragraph id="noGuaranteesDescription">
                Jstmemit is provided "as is". We can't promise that the bot will always be online, work without bugs, or
                that every meme will be funny, accurate or appropriate. The bot builds memes from whatever your channel
                feeds it, so weird or nonsensical results are part of the deal. We do not review or endorse them.
            </Paragraph>
        </div>
    </Section>

    <Section variant="light" headingId="liabilityHeading" descriptionId="liabilityDescription">
        <div slot="text" class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-333 flex-col gap-3">
            <Heading id="liabilityHeading"> 9. Liability </Heading>
            <Paragraph id="liabilityDescription">
                To the maximum extent the law allows, Wide Units and everyone working on Jstmemit aren't liable for any
                damage or loss that comes from using, or not being able to use, the bot or the website, including things
                like lost data or downtime.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph> If you're a consumer in the EU, you keep all the protections the law gives you. </Paragraph>
        </div>
    </Section>

    <Section variant="dark" headingId="terminationHeading" descriptionId="terminationDescription">
        <div slot="text" class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-333 flex-col gap-3">
            <Heading id="terminationHeading"> 10. Suspending or ending access </Heading>
            <Paragraph id="terminationDescription">
                We can suspend or remove access to the bot or website, for a whole server or a single person, if these
                terms are being broken or if something's harming other users, us, or third parties.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                It's as easy for you to stop using the bot. Disable the bot with <b>/enable</b> or kick it from your server
                whenever you like.
            </Paragraph>
        </div>
    </Section>

    <Section variant="light" headingId="changesHeading" descriptionId="changesDescription">
        <div slot="text" class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-333 flex-col gap-3">
            <Heading id="changesHeading"> 11. Changes to these terms </Heading>
            <Paragraph id="changesDescription">
                We may update these terms every now and then. The "Last updated" date at the top of this page always
                shows the current version, and we'll announce anything significant on our <a
                    href="https://discord.gg/THRnn8fhkZ"
                    target="_blank"
                    class="text-bubblegum-pink"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer">Support server</a
                > before it takes effect. Using the bot after a change means you agree with the new terms.
            </Paragraph>
        </div>
    </Section>

    <Section variant="dark" headingId="whoWeAreHeading" descriptionId="whoWeAreDescription">
        <div slot="text" class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-333 flex-col gap-3">
            <Heading id="controllerHeading"> 12. Who we are </Heading>
            <Paragraph id="controllerDescription">
                Jstmemit is operated by <b>Wide Units</b>, registered in the Netherlands with the Dutch Chamber of
                Commerce (KVK) under number <b>97552887</b>.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                General questions: <a class="text-bubblegum-pink" href="mailto:contact@jstmemit.com"
                    >contact@jstmemit.com</a
                ><br />
                Privacy and GDPR requests: <a class="text-bubblegum-pink" href="mailto:privacy@jstmemit.com"
                    >privacy@jstmemit.com</a
                >
            </Paragraph>
        </div>
    </Section>

    <Section variant="light" headingId="lawHeading" descriptionId="lawDescription">
        <div slot="text" class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-333 flex-col gap-3">
            <Heading id="lawHeading"> 13. Which laws apply </Heading>
            <Paragraph id="lawDescription">
                These terms are governed by Dutch law, and any disputes go to the Dutch courts, except where the law
                lets a consumer rely on the rules of their own country. Nothing here takes away the mandatory rights you
                have as a consumer in the EU.
            </Paragraph>
        </div>
    </Section>
</PageLayout>
